{title: How Majestic Is Your Name}
{subtitle: Psalm 8}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
LORD, our [Bb]Lord, how majestic is your [Eb]name in all the earth
[Gm]You have set [F]your splendor [Eb]above [F]the heavens
LORD, our [Bb]Lord, how majestic is your [Eb]name in all the [F]earth [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From the mouths of chil[F/A]dren and infants
You [Eb]have established strength because of your [Gm]foes
To si[F]lence the enemy and [Eb]the avenger
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]When I look [F/A]at your heav[Eb]ens, the work [Bb]of your fin[Gm]gers
The moon [F]and the stars [Eb]that you set [Gm]in place
What [F]is a human be[Eb]ing that you [Bb]remember him
[Gm]A son of [F]man that you [Eb]care for him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
LORD, [Bb]our Lord, how majestic is [Eb]your name in all the [Gm]earth
You have set [F]your splendor [Eb]above [F]the heavens
LORD, our [Bb]Lord, how majestic is your [Eb]name in all the [F]earth [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]You made him a [F]little lower than [Eb]God
[Gm]And crowned him with [F]glory and [Eb]honor
[Gm]You gave him do[F]minion over the [Eb]works of your [Bb]hands
[Gm]You put [F]everything under his [Eb]feet
[Gm]All the flocks [F]and herds, and [Eb]the beasts of [Bb]the field as well
[Gm]The birds of the [F]sky and the [Eb]fish of the [Bb]sea
[Gm]Whatever [F]passes a[Eb]long the [Bb]paths of the [Eb]seas
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
LORD, our [Bb]Lord, how majestic is your [Eb]name in all the earth
{end_of_verse}

